-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/0b494e51-907b-4e94-a8f6-e255621286cf
-- title:
--   Every successful capped uniform draw is in range
-- statement:
--   Let $\omega:\mathbb N\to\{0,1\}$ be a Boolean tape and let $T,v,c,a\in\mathbb N$. The bounded uniform sampler starts at cursor $c$, attempts at most $T$ rejection trials, and aims to return an integer below $v$. Whenever its optional result is $a$,
--
--   $$\operatorname{boundedUniform}(\omega,T,v,c).\mathrm{value}=\operatorname{some}(a)\quad\Longrightarrow\quad a<v.$$
--
--   This is a deterministic range guarantee for every tape, including the degenerate bounds $v=0$ and $v=1$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/ChainDrawAbortAttribution.lean#L17-L52

